%description:
The region error rates of each error model agree with its rate of the whole
signal. At a constant SNIR, the product of the success rates of the regions of
the header and the data must be equal to the success rate of the whole signal,
for each division of the parts into regions. Then a receiver that decides the
regions separately keeps the reception probability of a receiver that decides
the whole signal with one draw.

Each radio receives one frame. At the end of the reception, a checker computes
the rates of the error model of the receiver with an SNIR that has one value at
all times. For 141 SNIR values from -20 dB to 50 dB, it divides the header and
the data into 1, 2, and 7 regions, and compares the product with the rate of the
whole signal. It also checks that the two region rates agree: the region rate is
1 - (1 - bit error rate)^length. It prints the number of differences, and
whether some of the values gave a rate that is not 0 or 1.

The receivers: an APSK radio with its modulation model, and one with the
stochastic model and a fixed packet error rate, both with a preamble; an IEEE
802.15.4 radio, whose packet does not hold the header; and an IEEE 802.11 radio.
The runs change the mode and the error model of the IEEE 802.11 radio:

Run 0: DSSS at 1 Mbps, NIST.
Run 1: HR/DSSS at 11 Mbps, NIST.
Run 2: ERP-OFDM at 54 Mbps, NIST.
Run 3: ERP-OFDM at 6 Mbps, Yans.
Run 4: HT at 65 Mbps, NIST.
Run 5: HT at 65 Mbps, Yans.
Run 6: VHT at 693.3 Mbps, NIST.
Run 7: ERP-OFDM at 54 Mbps, the BER table model.

The stochastic model with a fixed bit error rate has no run: its rate of the
whole signal reads a bit model that a flat transmission does not have.

%file: test.cc
#include <cmath>

#include "inet/common/INETMath.h"
#include "inet/common/ProtocolTag_m.h"
#include "inet/common/Simsignals.h"
#include "inet/common/packet/Packet.h"
#include "inet/common/packet/chunk/ByteCountChunk.h"
#include "inet/physicallayer/wireless/apsk/packetlevel/ApskTransmission.h"
#include "inet/physicallayer/wireless/common/base/packetlevel/FlatReceiverBase.h"
#include "inet/physicallayer/wireless/common/contract/packetlevel/IRadio.h"
#include "inet/physicallayer/wireless/ieee80211/packetlevel/Ieee80211Radio.h"
#include "inet/physicallayer/wireless/ieee802154/packetlevel/Ieee802154Transmission.h"

namespace RegionErrorRates_2 {

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::physicallayer;

// Hands one packet of three chunks to the radio at the given time.
class TestSource : public cSimpleModule
{
  protected:
    virtual void initialize() override { scheduleAt(par("startTime"), new cMessage("start")); }
    virtual void handleMessage(cMessage *msg) override
    {
        auto packet = new Packet(getParentModule()->getName());
        for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++)
            packet->insertAtBack(makeShared<ByteCountChunk>(B(par("chunkLength").intValue()), i + 1));
        packet->addTag<PacketProtocolTag>()->setProtocol(&Protocol::ieee80211Mac);
        send(packet, "out");
        delete msg;
    }
};

Define_Module(TestSource);

// An SNIR that has one value at all times of a reception.
class FixedSnir : public ISnir
{
  protected:
    const IReception *reception;
    double value;

  public:
    FixedSnir(const IReception *reception, double value) : reception(reception), value(value) {}
    virtual std::ostream& printToStream(std::ostream& stream, int level, int evFlags = 0) const override { return stream << "FixedSnir"; }
    virtual const IReception *getReception() const override { return reception; }
    virtual const INoise *getNoise() const override { return nullptr; }
    virtual double getMin() const override { return value; }
    virtual double getMax() const override { return value; }
    virtual double getMean() const override { return value; }
    virtual double getMin(simtime_t startTime, simtime_t endTime) const override { return value; }
    virtual double getMax(simtime_t startTime, simtime_t endTime) const override { return value; }
    virtual double getMean(simtime_t startTime, simtime_t endTime) const override { return value; }
};

// Compares the region rates of the error model of the radio with its rate of the whole signal.
class RateChecker : public cSimpleModule, public cListener
{
  protected:
    int numDifferences = 0;

  protected:
    virtual void initialize() override { getModuleByPath("^.radio")->subscribe(receptionEndedSignal, this); }
    virtual void handleMessage(cMessage *msg) override { delete msg; }

    void addDifference(const char *text, double snir, int numRegions, double value, double expected)
    {
        if (numDifferences++ < 3)
            std::cout << par("label").stdstringValue() << ": " << text << " differs at " << math::fraction2dB(snir) << " dB with " << numRegions << " regions: " << value << " and " << expected << std::endl;
    }

    // Returns the product of the success rates of the regions of a part of length bits, which is divided into numRegions regions.
    double computePartSuccessRate(const IErrorModel *errorModel, const ISnir *snir, IRadioSignal::SignalPart part, int length, int numRegions)
    {
        auto reception = snir->getReception();
        simtime_t partStartTime = reception->getStartTime(part);
        simtime_t partDuration = reception->getDuration(part);
        double successRate = 1;
        for (int i = 0; i < numRegions; i++) {
            int startBit = (int64_t)length * i / numRegions;
            int endBit = (int64_t)length * (i + 1) / numRegions;
            if (startBit == endBit)
                continue;
            simtime_t startTime = partStartTime + partDuration * ((double)startBit / length);
            simtime_t endTime = partStartTime + partDuration * ((double)endBit / length);
            double rate = errorModel->computePacketErrorRate(snir, part, b(endBit - startBit), startTime, endTime);
            double bitErrorRate = errorModel->computeBitErrorRate(snir, part, b(endBit - startBit), startTime, endTime);
            double rateOfBits = 1 - std::pow(1 - bitErrorRate, endBit - startBit);
            if (!(std::fabs(rate - rateOfBits) <= 1e-9))
                addDifference("the region rate", snir->getMin(), numRegions, rate, rateOfBits);
            successRate *= 1 - rate;
        }
        return successRate;
    }

    virtual void receiveSignal(cComponent *source, simsignal_t signal, cObject *object, cObject *details) override
    {
        auto reception = check_and_cast<const IReception *>(object);
        auto transmission = reception->getTransmission();
        auto errorModel = check_and_cast<const FlatReceiverBase *>(reception->getReceiverRadio()->getReceiver())->getErrorModel();
        // the number of content bits of the header and the data
        int headerLength, dataLength;
        if (auto apskTransmission = dynamic_cast<const ApskTransmission *>(transmission)) {
            headerLength = apskTransmission->getHeaderLength().get<b>();
            dataLength = apskTransmission->getDataLength().get<b>();
        }
        else if (auto ieee802154Transmission = dynamic_cast<const Ieee802154Transmission *>(transmission)) {
            headerLength = ieee802154Transmission->getHeaderLength().get<b>();
            dataLength = ieee802154Transmission->getDataLength().get<b>();
        }
        else {
            auto phyHeader = Ieee80211Radio::peekIeee80211PhyHeaderAtFront(transmission->getPacket());
            headerLength = phyHeader->getChunkLength().get<b>();
            dataLength = b(phyHeader->getLengthField()).get<b>();
        }
        int numValues = 0;
        int numValuesBetween = 0;
        for (int i = -40; i <= 100; i++) {
            FixedSnir snir(reception, math::dB2fraction(i / 2.0));
            // the BER table model can give a value above 1
            double wholeSuccessRate = 1 - std::min(1.0, errorModel->computePacketErrorRate(&snir, IRadioSignal::SIGNAL_PART_WHOLE));
            numValues++;
            if (0.001 < wholeSuccessRate && wholeSuccessRate < 0.999)
                numValuesBetween++;
            for (int numRegions : {1, 2, 7}) {
                double successRate = computePartSuccessRate(errorModel, &snir, IRadioSignal::SIGNAL_PART_HEADER, headerLength, numRegions) *
                                     computePartSuccessRate(errorModel, &snir, IRadioSignal::SIGNAL_PART_DATA, dataLength, numRegions);
                bool isEqual = std::fabs(successRate - wholeSuccessRate) <= 1e-9 && (wholeSuccessRate < 1e-9 || std::fabs(successRate / wholeSuccessRate - 1) <= 1e-6);
                if (!isEqual)
                    addDifference("the success rate", snir.getMin(), numRegions, successRate, wholeSuccessRate);
            }
        }
        std::cout << par("label").stdstringValue() << ": " << numDifferences << " differences at " << numValues << " SNIR values, " << (numValuesBetween > 0 ? "some" : "none") << " with a rate between 0 and 1" << std::endl;
    }
};

Define_Module(RateChecker);

} // namespace RegionErrorRates_2

%file: test.ned

import inet.mobility.static.StationaryMobility;
import inet.physicallayer.wireless.common.contract.packetlevel.IRadio;
import inet.physicallayer.wireless.common.medium.ScalarRadioMedium;
import inet.physicallayer.wireless.ieee80211.packetlevel.Ieee80211ScalarRadioMedium;
import inet.physicallayer.wireless.ieee802154.packetlevel.Ieee802154NarrowbandScalarRadioMedium;

simple TestSource
{
    @class(TestSource);
    double startTime @unit(s);
    int chunkLength @unit(B);
    gates:
        output out;
}

simple RateChecker
{
    @class(RateChecker);
    string label;
    gates:
        input in;
}

module SenderNode
{
    parameters:
        @networkNode;
    submodules:
        mobility: StationaryMobility;
        radio: <> like IRadio;
        source: TestSource;
    connections allowunconnected:
        source.out --> radio.upperLayerIn;
}

module ReceiverNode
{
    parameters:
        @networkNode;
    submodules:
        mobility: StationaryMobility;
        radio: <> like IRadio;
        checker: RateChecker;
    connections allowunconnected:
        radio.upperLayerOut --> checker.in;
}

network Test
{
    submodules:
        apskMedium: ScalarRadioMedium;
        ieee802154Medium: Ieee802154NarrowbandScalarRadioMedium;
        ieee80211Medium: Ieee80211ScalarRadioMedium;
        apskSender: SenderNode;
        apskReceiver: ReceiverNode;
        apskStochasticSender: SenderNode;
        apskStochasticReceiver: ReceiverNode;
        ieee802154Sender: SenderNode;
        ieee802154Receiver: ReceiverNode;
        ieee80211Sender: SenderNode;
        ieee80211Receiver: ReceiverNode;
}

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
record-vector-results = false
network = Test
sim-time-limit = 50ms
ned-path = .;../../../../src

**.mobility.constraintAreaMinX = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinY = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinZ = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxX = 1000m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxY = 1000m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxZ = 0m
**.mobility.initFromDisplayString = false
**.mobility.initialY = 500m
**.mobility.initialZ = 0m
*.*Sender.mobility.initialX = 480m
*.*Receiver.mobility.initialX = 500m

**.radio.antenna.mobilityModule = "^.^.mobility"
*.*Sender.radio.initialRadioMode = "transmitter"
*.*Receiver.radio.initialRadioMode = "receiver"
*.*Medium.backgroundNoise.power = -110dBm

# the APSK radios, with the modulation model and with the stochastic model
*.apsk*.radio.typename = "ApskScalarRadio"
*.apsk*.radio.radioMediumModule = "apskMedium"
*.apsk*.radio.centerFrequency = 2.4GHz
*.apsk*.radio.bandwidth = 2MHz
*.apsk*.radio.transmitter.bitrate = 2Mbps
*.apsk*.radio.transmitter.modulation = "BPSK"
*.apsk*.radio.transmitter.preambleDuration = 100us
*.apsk*.radio.transmitter.headerLength = 96b
*.apsk*.radio.transmitter.power = 10mW
*.apsk*.radio.receiver.energyDetection = -90dBm
*.apsk*.radio.receiver.sensitivity = -85dBm
*.apsk*.radio.receiver.snirThreshold = 10dB
*.apskStochasticReceiver.radio.receiver.errorModel.typename = "StochasticErrorModel"
*.apskStochasticReceiver.radio.receiver.errorModel.packetErrorRate = 0.3
# the receiver also reports the bit and symbol error rates of each reception
*.apskStochasticReceiver.radio.receiver.errorModel.bitErrorRate = 0.001
*.apskStochasticReceiver.radio.receiver.errorModel.symbolErrorRate = 0.001
*.apskSender.source.startTime = 0s
*.apskStochasticSender.source.startTime = 20ms
*.apsk*.source.chunkLength = 500B
*.apskReceiver.checker.label = "apsk"
*.apskStochasticReceiver.checker.label = "apsk stochastic"

# the IEEE 802.15.4 radios
*.ieee802154*.radio.typename = "Ieee802154NarrowbandScalarRadio"
*.ieee802154*.radio.radioMediumModule = "ieee802154Medium"
*.ieee802154Sender.source.startTime = 0s
*.ieee802154Sender.source.chunkLength = 30B
*.ieee802154Receiver.checker.label = "ieee802154"

# the IEEE 802.11 radios, with the variants of the runs
*.ieee80211*.radio.typename = "Ieee80211ScalarRadio"
*.ieee80211*.radio.radioMediumModule = "ieee80211Medium"
*.ieee80211*.radio.opMode = ${opMode="b", "b", "g(erp)", "g(erp)", "n(mixed-2.4Ghz)", "n(mixed-2.4Ghz)", "ac", "g(erp)" ! run}
*.ieee80211*.radio.transmitter.bitrate = ${bitrate=1Mbps, 11Mbps, 54Mbps, 6Mbps, 65Mbps, 65Mbps, 693.3Mbps, 54Mbps ! run}
*.ieee80211*.radio.bandName = ${band="2.4 GHz", "2.4 GHz", "2.4 GHz", "2.4 GHz", "2.4 GHz", "2.4 GHz", "5 GHz (mapped 20 MHz)", "2.4 GHz" ! run}
*.ieee80211*.radio.antenna.numAntennas = ${antennas=1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 8, 1 ! run}
*.ieee80211*.radio.receiver.errorModel.typename = ${model="Ieee80211NistErrorModel", "Ieee80211NistErrorModel", "Ieee80211NistErrorModel", "Ieee80211YansErrorModel", "Ieee80211NistErrorModel", "Ieee80211YansErrorModel", "Ieee80211NistErrorModel", "Ieee80211BerTableErrorModel" ! run}
*.ieee80211*.radio.receiver.errorModel.berTableFile = "../../../statistical/files/per_table_80211g_Trivellato.dat"
*.ieee80211*.radio.receiver.errorModel.opMode = "g(erp)"
*.ieee80211*.radio.channelNumber = 0
*.ieee80211*.radio.transmitter.power = 100mW
*.ieee80211Sender.source.startTime = 0s
*.ieee80211Sender.source.chunkLength = 100B
*.ieee80211Receiver.checker.label = "ieee80211 run ${run=0..7}"

%extraargs: -r 0..7

%contains: stdout
apsk: 0 differences at 141 SNIR values, some with a rate between 0 and 1
%contains: stdout
apsk stochastic: 0 differences at 141 SNIR values, some with a rate between 0 and 1
%contains: stdout
ieee802154: 0 differences at 141 SNIR values, some with a rate between 0 and 1
%contains: stdout
ieee80211 run 0: 0 differences at 141 SNIR values, some with a rate between 0 and 1
%contains: stdout
ieee80211 run 1: 0 differences at 141 SNIR values, some with a rate between 0 and 1
%contains: stdout
ieee80211 run 2: 0 differences at 141 SNIR values, some with a rate between 0 and 1
%contains: stdout
ieee80211 run 3: 0 differences at 141 SNIR values, some with a rate between 0 and 1
%contains: stdout
ieee80211 run 4: 0 differences at 141 SNIR values, some with a rate between 0 and 1
%contains: stdout
ieee80211 run 5: 0 differences at 141 SNIR values, some with a rate between 0 and 1
%contains: stdout
ieee80211 run 6: 0 differences at 141 SNIR values, some with a rate between 0 and 1
%contains: stdout
ieee80211 run 7: 0 differences at 141 SNIR values, some with a rate between 0 and 1

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
